{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01WXRg7cZp7UszgDP1yaLmSU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task 2 is complete. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n### Changes made to `task_discovery.py`:\n\n1. **Improved `_extract_test_traceback()`** (line ~231):\n   - Added collection of assertion detail lines (lines prefixed with `E ` by pytest)\n   - Ensured the last 5 lines of the traceback are always included (these typically contain the assertion and location info)\n   - If assertion lines exist but aren't in the last 5 lines, they are appended to ensure assertion details are never lost\n\n2. **Added `_extract_traceback_location()`** helper (line ~281):\n   - Uses a regex (`_TRACEBACK_LOC_RE`) to parse pytest traceback lines like `tests/test_foo.py:5: AssertionError`\n   - Returns the last matching `(source_file, line_number)` tuple from the traceback, which is typically the failing assertion location\n\n3. **Updated `_discover_test_failures()`** (line ~325):\n   - After extracting the per-test traceback, calls `_extract_traceback_location()` to get the file path and line number\n   - Sets `source_file` and `line_number` on the `Task` so Claude can jump directly to the relevant code\n\nAll 919 tests pass."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":291,"cache_read_input_tokens":41320,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":291,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49c99b86-4be3-464a-a24b-94401b602357","uuid":"8ce3d557-3d2a-4a53-b6f7-20ca0ae1ce86"}
