 30→feedback.py          # Watch feedback/ dir for developer task files\n    31→state.py             # Persist history to state/history.json\n    32→cycle_state.py       # Live cycle state for dashboard visibility\n    33→state_lock.py        # Thread-safe StateManager wrapper for parallel mode\n    34→safety.py            # Lock file, failure counters, disk/rate/cost checks (~540 lines)\n    35→shared.py            # Shared prompt builders, commit message helpers (~680 lines)\n    36→process_utils.py     # Subprocess utilities with process group kill\n    37→conflict_resolver.py # AI-powered merge conflict resolution\n    38→coordinator.py       # Parallel coordinator\n    39→worker.py            # Parallel worker in git worktrees\n    40→dashboard.py         # Web dashboard\n    41→task_queue.py        # Task approval queue\n    42→notifications.py     # Notification system\n    43→telemetry.py         # Metrics computation\n    44→cost_predictor.py    # Cost prediction\n    45→llm_judges.py        # LLM-based code review judges\n    46→provider_runner.py   # Abstract runner supporting multiple providers\n    47→session_manager.py   # Session recovery for orphaned worktrees\n    48→structured_logging.py # JSON logging support\n    49→context_monitor.py   # Context window usage tracking\n    50→config_tuner.py      # Auto-tuning configuration\n    51→```\n    52→\n    53→## Core Loop Flow\n    54→\n    55→1. Pre-flight safety checks (lock, disk, memory, rate limit, cost, failure count)\n    56→2. Check `feedback/` for developer-submitted priority tasks\n    57→3. If no feedback: auto-discover tasks (test failures, lint, TODOs, coverage, quality, Claude ideas)\n    58→4. De-duplicate against recent history\n    59→5. Pick highest-priority task (or adaptive batch)\n    60→6. Record git snapshot\n    61→7. Invoke Claude Code with task prompt (or multi-agent pipeline)\n    62→8. Check changed files (count limit, protected files)\n    63→9. Validate: run tests, lint, build (short-circuit on failure)\n    64→10. If invalid: retry with failure output (up to max_validation_retries)\n    65→11. If valid: commit; If all retries exhausted: rollback\n    66→12. Record cycle in state/history.json\n    67→13. Sleep and repeat\n    68→\n    69→## Key Patterns and Conventions\n    70→\n    71→- **One external dep**: `pyyaml`. Everything else is stdlib.\n    72→- **File-based everything**: state is JSON, feedback is text files, config is YAML.\n    73→- **Claude prompt says \"do NOT commit\"** -- the orchestrator handles all git operations.\n    74→- **Self-improvement mode**: when `self_improve: true`, syntax-checks `.py` files before commit.\n    75→- **Shared prompt builders**: `shared.py` contains `build_task_prompt()`, `build_plan_prompt()`, `build_execute_prompt()`, `build_retry_prompt()` used by both orchestrator and worker.\n    76→- **Task types**: `test_failure` (priority 2), `lint` (priority 2), `todo` (priority 3), `coverage` (priority 4), `claude_idea` (priority 4), `quality` (priority 5), `feedback` (priority 1).\n    77→- **Adaptive priority**: tasks from historically high-success-rate sources get boosted priority.\n    78→- **Circuit breaker**: in `claude_runner.py`, blocks API calls after repeated failures with exponential backoff.\n    79→- **Process group kill**: all subprocesses use `start_new_session=True` and are killed via process group to prevent orphans.\n    80→\n    81→## Key Interfaces\n    82→\n    83→### Task dataclass (`task_discovery.py`)\n    84→```python\n    85→@dataclass\n    86→class Task:\n    87→    description: str\n    88→    priority: int       # 1=highest, 5=lowest\n    89→    source: str         # \"test_failure\", \"lint\", \"todo\", \"coverage\", \"quality\", \"feedback\", \"claude_idea\"\n    90→    source_file: Optional[str] = None\n    91→    line_number: Optional[int] = None\n    92→    context: str = \"\"   # rich context: tracebacks, file snippets, error details\n    93→    task_id: str = \"